        "id": "ch1_7-1",
        "text": "Summary\nWe\u2019ve done a lot in this chapter. We\u2019ve discussed what PowerShell is and what it\u2019s suited for, such as\nproducing short pieces of automation code quickly and easily. We\u2019ve downloaded and installed it in\na few different ways, specifically by installing it from an .msi file and extracting it from a .zip file.\nWe\u2019ve tried some different ways of starting it using the built-in shell, and finally, we\u2019ve looked at three\nuseful cmdlets: Get-Command , for finding cmdlets that we might use, Get-Help , for understanding\nhow to use them, and Get-Member , to understand what output those cmdlets produce.\nIn the next chapter, we will explore how cmdlets work, explore parameters and syntax, and look at a\nuseful application for working interactively with PowerShell: Windows Terminal.",
